  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Fresh-task resource check",
      "items": [
        "check fresh task resources: a fresh dispatch is checked before workspace, provider or supervisor preparation. Existing or uncertain task IDs skip it.",
        "pressure: retry_later: confirmed pressure (3 sustained intervals, or critical memory) refuses the new request with task_record not_created, retry_later and retry_after_seconds. Nothing is queued or retried.",
        "unknown + warning: an unavailable metric never refuses by itself. If no independent pressure is confirmed, the check lets admission continue with resource_admission unknown and a warning; later admission steps may still fail.",
        "refresh only if stale or target changed: before task creation the check reruns only when it is older than 5 s or the execution target changed. A late refusal still creates no task.",
        "Running tasks, status, collect, cancel and existing-task recovery are never checked. Nothing is persisted, killed or throttled."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Grouped source owners",
      "items": [
        "Control is app composition calling tasklifecycle behavior. resourceadmission owns sampling and the pure pressure decision; tasklifecycle owns the fresh-task gate.",
        "supervisor owns binding and gates; Pueue owns queue rows. guardian owns lifetime; execution owns provider Start/Wait and sealing.",
        "Status uses ObserveTaskSupervisor. A shared-lease canonical generation check precedes cached or fresh task rows; optional repair remains mutation-gated.",
        "prepare candidate: app composes tasklifecycle; task creation calls admission.Prepare. Managed runtime-only profiles admit a static capability contract without version/help workers.",
        "prepare supervisor: supervisor owns binding and submission policy; Pueue owns the private queue and row state. Legacy logical binding adoption is create-once and precedes scheduling changes.",
        "strict, when required: This is the conditional phase inside admission.Prepare: candidate inspection is finalized only when runtime checks were not deferred. The grouped participant includes sealed inspection workers.",
        "persist immutable task: tasklifecycle requests creation; TaskDir writes brief.md, task.json and meta.json before supervisor submission.",
        "persist numeric receipt: The staged submission invokes tasklifecycle\u2019s commit callback, which calls TaskDir.RecordSupervisorReceipt. The queue row is still stashed.",
        "enqueue that exact row: The Pueue adapter enqueues only after the receipt callback succeeds; commit failure leaves the stashed row recoverable."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Publication authority",
      "items": [
        "TaskDir calls the predicate on sealed evidence and commits outcome.json. Only that record establishes a terminal verdict.",
        "The guardian\u2019s termination and exact worker Wait are separate durable lifetime facts.",
        "Full maintenance sends all current rows to the same durable authorizer. With terminal events enabled, event-only starts from inbox IDs.",
        "scope intent + registration: The guardian writes intent before scope creation and registration before starting its managed worker.",
        "identity acknowledged: The worker cannot receive its hello acknowledgement until its observed identity is durable.",
        "fresh runtime preflight: Admission reconstructs the candidate, probes the current runtime inside the guardian scope and finite budget, finalizes strictly, and matches the admitted contract.",
        "Start after strict match: Strict profile matching precedes Start. The guardian records each observed native launch before acknowledging it (internal/guardian/control.go:198-225).",
        "termination + empty scope: The guardian proves the native scope empty and persists termination before acknowledging close.",
        "seal evidence; finalize: execution seals provider.exit and calls TaskDir.Finalize only after successful lifetime closure.",
        "final outcome: TaskDir commits outcome.json as committed or rejected, then returns it to execution. Payload files are evidence, not terminal authority.",
        "persist exact child Wait: The guardian retains scope and owner until termination and its exact managed-worker Wait disposition are durable."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Observation and continuation",
      "items": [
        "observe and reconcile: tasklifecycle can recover the exact stashed row or publish an existing seal. A typed pre-mutation refusal during stashed recovery triggers fresh same-client observation. Each attempt replaces derived maintenance deferral; no new provider turn.",
        "active owner: terminate scope: The active guardian reads the durable request and persists native termination proof.",
        "else, lease: stop row: Direct queue stopping requires the task lifetime lease, so no guardian can concurrently own or launch the provider.",
        "linked successor in caller scope: continue loads the predecessor, runs one resource check, then dispatches a new task in the current caller's environment and supervisor control. Predecessor records decide only compatibility."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Optional workspaces",
      "items": [
        "This sequence shows an ordinary provider task. workspaces coordinates optional Git isolation and finite helpers on the same supervised path.",
        "Workspace journals keep independent capture receipts; the lead verifies and explicitly releases or forgets the retained checkout."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Live acceptance",
      "items": [
        "Native acceptance is auth-gated; BLOCKED is neutral."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
